id: pm-case-jow8
title: Keep published dependency updates in the generated changelog
description: "Published dependency bullets disappear when a changelog entry point regenerates history without --dependency-updates. Every package changelog invocation must pass that flag, and a regression must fail if an entry point drops it."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-24T01:03:00.551Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T01:05:50.184Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Every package changelog entry point passes --dependency-updates.; Regeneration keeps the dependency bullets main already published, and a disposable revert of the flag fails the new regression."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T01:03:15.528Z",codex-agent,"Every package changelog script invoked pm-changelog without --dependency-updates. The fix adds the flag to changelog, changelog:full, changelog:check, and release:notes, and a regression that fails if any of those entry points drops it."
  "2026-11-24T01:05:31.354Z",codex-agent,"Regeneration restored 10 published dependency bullets versus main and dropped none. The one bullet already on main remained. The current release-notes window has no dependency bullets. Removing only the flag from the package scripts in a disposable copy fails the new regression with an assertion on changelog. Typecheck, lint, identity, privacy tests, changelog check, and the package changelog tests passed."
